  "notes": "⛔ **The low end is the entry, and it is why `drums.bass808` is explicitly null here.** The research: \"a plucked, filter-enveloped analog synth bass moving in 8ths or 16ths rather than a sustained 808 — this is the distinguishing low-end parameter for the entry\". Inheriting `trap-soul`'s 808 would have made the bass generator return nothing and handed him the lane's drone, so the 808 is killed and a real `bassline` block is authored with `rhythm` `offbeat_8ths`. The rest follows the same sentence: \"the fastest habitual band in this section, and the one place where half-time is *not* the default\" — 100–124 straight, `halfTime` false, snare on 2&4, four-on-the-floor kick in the chorus and closed 16th hats. The harmony is \"closer to 80s synth-pop than to trap\": 4-bar cycles that genuinely move, borrowed major chords as hooks, so the triad share climbs and a major family carries real weight. The \"additive electronic form\" of the arrangement is the prechorus/breakdown structure. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are the swing amount (0.5, i.e. straight, read off \"four-on-the-floor… straight 8th kick\"), every drum probability and density, and the bassline's glide and passing-tone set. ⚠ `confidence` is medium, mirroring the entry. ⚠ `session.bpm.mode` is **INFERRED**: the number is not stated in the entry, and it is an authored centre of gravity inside the band the entry does state. ⚠ **`session.keys` is INFERRED.** The entry's Keys line describes the harmonic grammar but names no key centre, so these values and their weights are an authored choice — no key in this set is stated in the research.",
